<p>U.S. officials say Russia has shared intelligence with Iran that could help Tehran identify and strike U.S. military assets in the Middle East. Officials speaking anonymously stressed that U.S. intelligence has not found evidence that Russia is directing Iran on how to use the information. Some reporting says Tehran has used intelligence from Moscow to support retaliatory drone and missile attacks during the ongoing regional conflict. U.S. messaging has stayed measured: one assessment said the sharing is “not making any difference,” and another report said officials are “not concerned,” even as the disclosure highlights escalation risks for U.S. forces operating in the region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/M1f0H2EGs1qHpL_aqRollHrxZlJmFwAcJar2nLtW6YSbLwP92VWnwSAfErnhb9nHDVhNUND5i_C-V3eF4_tpdEV1L12cB54T93SjTlSrPX4HB36LrhQK4beVigvnqQEz80NIh0xAcwjCGE2LgkAXEH9U7O0MoF-3OO4nPS_FxYovcd8mbYXcpwxB2sHxx8f3SW5nFY-oYWiKddTMJD7e31jf0C1jR92YpwMsDE0' alt='Russia’s Moscow embassy scene amid the Iran crisis, as reports describe Russia-Iran contacts.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>How it may be used and when it began: Reporting said Tehran has used intelligence from Moscow to support retaliatory drone and missile attacks, and that the sharing began after the fighting started—an early sign of Moscow’s involvement.</li><li>Reporting trail / characterization: U.S. officials told RFE/RL they were confirming earlier reporting and described Moscow as playing a “substantial,” if indirect, role in the widening conflict.</li><li>Wider context: Several outlets said Russia is among the few countries to maintain friendly ties with Iran, despite years of isolation linked to Tehran’s nuclear programme and regional proxy relationships.</li></ul><blockquote>We are in dialogue with the Iranian side, with representatives of the Iranian leadership, and will certainly continue this dialogue - Dmitry Peskov</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. officials (intelligence assessment): Officials said Russia shared information that could help Iran strike U.S. assets, while cautioning that U.S. intelligence has not found evidence Russia is telling Iran how to use it. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3345785/us-says-russian-intelligence-iran-not-making-any-difference-war'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>U.S. officials (public posture): U.S. officials publicly played down the reports, saying they were not concerned by the alleged Russian assistance. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-not-concerned-by-reports-russia-aiding-irans-targeting'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Kremlin: Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said Russia is in “dialogue” with representatives of Iran’s leadership and plans to keep those contacts going. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-war-russia-intel-sources/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Financial Times framing: The FT reported that Tehran has used intelligence shared by Moscow to help carry out retaliatory drone and missile attacks on U.S. positions in the region. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/19be57d7-6299-4a1d-b761-3d699d07de94'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3345785/us-says-russian-intelligence-iran-not-making-any-difference-war'>US says Russian intelligence for Iran ‘not making any difference’ in war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/19be57d7-6299-4a1d-b761-3d699d07de94'>Russia is helping Iran to target US military assets in Middle East</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russia-has-provided-iran-with-information-that-can-help-iran-strike-us-military-ap-sources-say/article70713538.ece'>Russia has provided Iran with information that can help Iran strike U.S. military, AP sources say</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/russia-helping-iran-with-intelligence-on-the-location-of-us-forces-in-west-asia-report-13987037.html'>Russia helping Iran with intelligence on the location of US forces in West Asia: Report</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-war-russia-intel-sources/'>Russia providing intel to Iran about U.S. positions, sources say</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/russia-has-aided-irans-targeting-us-military-gulf-officials'>Russia has aided Iran’s targeting US military in Gulf: Officials</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/russia-iran--intel-targeting-us-israel-war/33697849.html'>US Officials Confirm Russia Providing Targeting Intelligence To Iran In Middle East War</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-06-0800/world-russia-has-provided-iran-information-can-help-tehran-strike-us-military-ap-sources-say'>Russia has provided Iran with information that can help Tehran strike US military, AP sources say</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/07/russia-allegedly-provided-iran-with-intel-that-could-help-it-strike-us-military-sources-sa'>Russia allegedly provided Iran with intel that could help it strike US military, sources say</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/iran-receiving-intelligence-support-from-russia-officials-say'>Iran receiving intelligence support from Russia, officials say</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-not-concerned-by-reports-russia-aiding-irans-targeting'>US ‘not concerned’ by reports Russia aiding Iran’s targeting</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>